# TODO - Search pruning and state canonicalization

## Objective

Develop exact pruning, dominance rules, partial-equivalence checks, canonical
states, admissible heuristics, and profile-aware constraints before relying on
raw hardware scale.

## Acceptance

- Every pruning/dominance/canonicalization rule is justified by equivalence or
  admissibility evidence and has adversarial tests that would catch an unsound
  discarded state.
- Pruning evidence reports raw candidates, rejected candidates, survivors, prune
  fraction, and effective branching by search depth or declared difficulty. A
  strong aggregate prune percentage cannot hide a collapse toward unpruned
  branching in later layers.
- The implementation may combine the completed exact mathematics base with safe
  dynamic reachability, dominance, memoization, verifier-specific reasoning, or
  other independently justified filters; no single source of pruning is assumed
  sufficient at every depth.
- A CPU/reference path remains sufficient for correctness, and accelerator
  failure/unavailability changes performance rather than semantic acceptance.
- The work states a falsifiable question or hypothesis, an explicit baseline,
  and an observation that would reject or materially weaken the proposed
  technique before performance conclusions are accepted.
- If executable algorithm research is required, the stable ID is mirrored under
  `docs/research/algorithms/<id>/` and `algorithms/<id>/`; ordinary product
  engineering is not forced into that mirror.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `accelerator/`, `algorithms/`,
  `optimizer/`, `benchmarks/accelerator/`, `tests/optimizer/`.
- Required evidence: CPU/reference differential results, device/resource
  metadata, failure/fallback tests, and benchmark samples for claimed speedups.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `deterministic-cpu-optimizer`,
  `malbolge-specific-optimization-mathematics`.
- The mathematics prerequisite is a completed bounded milestone with 226 exact
  reductions. If retained traces show residual symmetry causing late-depth
  branching growth, targeted higher-arity mathematics is escalated to
  `high-arity-synthesis-symmetry-pruning` instead of reopening the P1 milestone.
- Active exploratory evidence: exact pre-identity byte duplicate pruning retains
  stable first representatives and rejects every stronger equality shortcut. The
  duplicate-rich fixture maps eight inputs to five representatives, while the
  all-unique null fixture remains four-to-four. One-byte and prefix/length
  adversarial cases remain distinct. The deterministic CPU enumerator now
  applies
  an independent Python implementation of the same exact relation before logical
  identity; duplicate corpus bytes roundtrip unchanged, while budget is consumed
  only by stable first representatives. Python production tests and the five
  Rust

  research adversarials both pass. The hardware-neutral generic layer is also
  now bounded by a maximality argument: any two byte-distinct payloads can be
  separated by a legal trusted verifier, so no coarser universal equivalence is
  sound without profile-, semantics-, or verifier-specific proof obligations.
  This is correctness/evaluation-count evidence only; stronger canonicalization,
  dominance, admissible heuristics, and preregistered performance evidence
  remain
  open.
